<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ephialtes (Athenian statesman)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 461 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ephialtes was an Athenian democratic politician who in 462/461 BCE carried reforms that stripped the aristocratic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/areopagus">Council of the Areopagus</a> of most of its political and judicial powers, transferring them to the Council of Five Hundred, the Assembly and the popular courts. He was assassinated soon afterwards, and his associate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pericles">Pericles</a> became the leading figure of the democracy.</p></div>
